cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use these notebooks or reports, please cite them as below.

type: software

title: "SA_Management: Management and Curation of EarthPortal Resources"

version: "v1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-11-12"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23417011"

abstract: >-
  Jupyter notebooks that build a dated state of the art of the semantic
  artefacts hosted on an OntoPortal portal (EarthPortal by default). They
  collect the catalogue and the O'FAIRe assessments through the portal API,
  turn the OntoPortal Metadata Guidelines into a machine-readable profile,
  and write one audit per artefact in two parts, FAIRness (O'FAIRe) and
  compliance with the guidelines, with prioritised actions and who can take
  them. Each audit is saved as a page and as a JSON file for programs. The
  repository also holds the reports and slides written during an internship
  at CNRS / Data Terra.

